.TH WEACTTERM 1 "October 2026" "WeAct35 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weactterm \- foreground FS35 PTY terminal using libvterm and FreeType
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weactterm
.RB [ --dry-run | --run ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
weactterm runs a shell or command in a PTY, lets libvterm own the current
terminal screen, and rasterises it with FreeType on FS35.  It supports FS35
only, not FS096.  No argument is a finite memory-only demonstration; --run is
the only mode that opens USB and performs full managed FS35 initialisation
(orientation 02 and black clear).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Memory-only PTY mode; no device is opened.
.TP
.B --run
Guarded FS35 hardware mode.  Without --command it starts interactive $SHELL,
falling back to /bin/sh.
.TP
.BI --command " CMD"
Run /bin/sh -c CMD in the child PTY.
.TP
.BI --device " PATH"
Choose an absolute matching CDC ACM/by-id path.
.TP
.BI --serial " SERIAL"
Require a matching USB serial.
.TP
.B --allow-unknown-occupancy
Limited permission-only occupancy override after identity checks; known busy,
identity, namespace and scanner failures remain fatal.
.TP
.B --ctrl-c-to-pty
Forward Ctrl+C to the PTY.  Otherwise Ctrl+C exits; Ctrl+] always exits.
.TP
.B --perf-stats
Print host PTY, rendering and transfer counters on exit, not LCD latency.
.TP
.BI --font-size " tiny|small|normal|large|xlarge"
Select fixed DejaVu Sans Mono grids: tiny 96x32, small 80x26, normal 60x20
(default), large 40x13, xlarge 30x10.
.TP
.B --compression off|fastlz
Default off.  FastLZ is explicit FS35 presenter compression; no fallback follows
a transport failure.
.TP
.BI --brightness " 0..50"
Set FS35 backlight after successful init; omission leaves it unchanged.
.TP
.BI --brightness-fade-ms " 0..65535"
Requires --brightness.  Effective fade is capped at 5000 ms.
.SH TERMINAL OPERATION
The child receives TERM=xterm and LC_ALL=C.UTF-8.  UTF-8, cursor and supported
control sequences are handled by libvterm.  Enter, Backspace, Tab, arrows,
Home/End, Insert/Delete, Page Up/Down and F1 through F4 are mapped; unknown
escape sequences are forwarded.  There is no scrollback UI, mouse protocol,
runtime font selection or promise of a complete desktop terminal emulator.
Frames are coalesced and capped at 20 fps; changed terminal tiles may be sent
as regions, while first/costly changes are full frames.
.SH TERMINATION
Terminal attributes are restored.  The child/foreground group receives SIGHUP
on closure and is eventually killed if it does not exit.  Child normal status
is returned; Ctrl+] gives 130, handled signals give 128 plus signal, and
internal/render/USB failures give 2.  Disconnects stop rather than reconnect.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
weactterm --dry-run --command "printf 'preview\\n'" --font-size large
weactterm --run --device /dev/serial/by-id/usb-WeAct_Studio_Display_FS_V1_YOUR_ID-if00 \
  --command 'uname -a; sleep 2'
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR weact-list (1),
.BR weact-cli (1),
.BR libweact (3)
